[00:08.16] I'm just driftwood on the river, floating down the tide
[00:15.20] I don't care where this old river carries me
[00:22.90] I'll keep drifting just because my heart is broken inside
[00:30.78] And I'm tired of wishing for what cannot be.
[00:39.14] I may meet some little driftwood, lost as same as I
[00:46.52] Share a handshake and a tender tear or two
[00:54.32] But it's always good luck, now we've got to say goodbye
[01:02.08] I must wander on to keep my randezvous.
[01:25.70] --- Instrumental ---
[01:25.70] Though I drift through town and city I can never stay
[01:32.50] For I find no place to call my home sweet home
[01:39.80] I don't ask for help or pitty I'll just go my way
[01:48.24] All I'm praying for is peace to dream alone.
[01:56.60] I'm just driftwood on the river and I'm drifting on
[02:04.24] Till this weary river meets the deep blue sea
[02:11.72] Where the deep blue sea may help me to forget someone
[02:19.60] Yes the careless one who has forgotten me.
[02:27.62] In my heart I don't feel bitter over what has been
[02:34.52] I feel sorry for the one I must forget
[02:42.52] And instead of being someone with the world to win
[02:50.46] I'm just driftwood on the river of regret...
